{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>Your eyes have seen.</b> It refers back to what is above — למען תחיון ובאתם וירשתם — for your eyes have seen that <b>every man who went after Baal Peor, HaShem destroyed him</b>, even though they were worthy of being among those who would enter the land, as it is written: ויהי כאשר תמו כל אנשי המלחמה למות מקרב העם ויאמר ה׳ אלי וגו׳, and afterward they came to Shittim, and there they died in the plague of Baal Peor." "<b>In Baal Peor.</b> On account of Baal Peor. And there are many like this." "<b>HaShem your Elohim destroyed from your midst.</b> But you — the ones who cleave to HaShem your Elohim; therefore you are all alive today. And since they were near Beth Peor, he warned first concerning idolatry."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:51:34.513497515Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}